SELECT SYSTEM$DRAFT_GLOSSARY_TERM('{"name": "Game", "domainName": "Game Catalog", "itemKind": "ENTITY", "description": "A video game. Master record GAME_CATALOG.GAMES (GAME_ID, GAME_NAME, RELEASE_DATE as DATE, STATUS, POV). The Sales system calls a game a TITLE: GAME_SALES.TITLES (TITLE_ID 5001-5090 is a Sales-only key; CATALOG_GAME_ID links to GAMES.GAME_ID but is NULL for some titles; RELEASE_DATE is text YYYYMMDD). Store codes are in GAME_SALES.TITLE_CODE_XREF. 8 Sales names differ: GT7 = Gran Turismo 7, Ghost of Yotei = Ghost of Yōtei, DEATH STRANDING 2 = Death Stranding 2: On the Beach, Spider-Man 2 = Marvel''s Spider-Man 2, God of War Ragnarok = God of War Ragnarök, Ratchet and Clank Rift Apart = Ratchet & Clank: Rift Apart, The Last of Us Part 1 = The Last of Us Part I, Demons Souls = Demon''s Souls. Match a Title to a Game with the Game Identity Match Rule. GRAIN: one game is sold as many SKUs (Digital Products); count games, not products. To count games with sales, resolve each sale to a catalog GAME_ID first, then COUNT(DISTINCT GAME_ID).", "synonyms": ["Title", "Store Title", "Product Title"]}');
